{"id": "EUVD-2026-101035", "enisaUuid": "605b63b3-030b-3807-b45a-ff0e553815ba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Use memset_io() to clear QLAFX00 request ring slot\n\nFor QLAFX00 the request ring is ioremapped device I/O memory\n(ha->iobase + req_que_off), not DMA-coherent RAM, which is why the rest\nof the FX00 path accesses it through memcpy_toio() and the wrt_reg_*\nhelpers. __qla2x00_alloc_iocbs() however zeroed the producer slot with a\nplain memset(). On architectures such as ARM64 a regular memset() may\nemit unaligned or block-zeroing instructions (e.g. DC ZVA) that are\ninvalid on Device memory, leading to a synchronous external abort.\n\nUse memset_io() to clear the slot for QLAFX00, matching the I/O\naccessors used elsewhere on this ring. Other adapters keep the plain\nmemset() on their DMA-coherent rings. The zero-fill is retained for FX00\nbecause its IOCB builders (e.g. qlafx00_fxdisc_iocb()) copy only part of\nthe entry and rely on the unused tail being pre-zeroed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:25:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2df8c8630904794100189fa3d70598642e1877ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53eb96c244d150dfb8cc4b5b0492ab53755f3701", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ee6dfd922fafd508f6bde16de30dd2db796b7a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e41d28d9a242c4005b7d01a7ee7769405a6a2c2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/626e44f3d8a924a97a3848a9fd45833947e081e9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98386", "GHSA-xqf4-fcfm-9wq2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0420eee7-2b96-32de-8359-05872ea6fd26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0c6aad47-e984-308e-8b07-966f7a1bea55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ae6d9c7eb1004bc134813287010d57a863ba13b <53eb96c244d150dfb8cc4b5b0492ab53755f3701"}, {"id": "26c3da72-3122-36c2-bad2-4176ecb5b35e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ae6d9c7eb1004bc134813287010d57a863ba13b <626e44f3d8a924a97a3848a9fd45833947e081e9"}, {"id": "2784399f-3c41-3c20-8801-a1ad9632d2e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ae6d9c7eb1004bc134813287010d57a863ba13b <6ee6dfd922fafd508f6bde16de30dd2db796b7a7"}, {"id": "3b9daaa8-5c35-3e71-83c5-34aa8fe616a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "3cfcbab0-fe46-34fd-8264-7fe126556454", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3dea6486-47bd-35b2-b825-e13d9314b562", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "596535d9-aa3d-30df-8642-88a99d74c3ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ae1acb62-fdd5-3d26-94de-0aaad6f08c34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "c6652cbb-c498-3fe9-9f24-77766ba7d871", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ae6d9c7eb1004bc134813287010d57a863ba13b <2df8c8630904794100189fa3d70598642e1877ce"}, {"id": "f083303a-359d-3d94-8e6c-d90d9370a125", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.10"}, {"id": "f60a5e79-9126-333b-9b1f-d872a4c6bf72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8ae6d9c7eb1004bc134813287010d57a863ba13b <e41d28d9a242c4005b7d01a7ee7769405a6a2c2e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1214741c-93f5-3fb8-8e42-9e1a515f63b7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}